es you at the least. Charmed, you are the bestest of friends, everything you say is a good idea. Green eyes you are equal to her husband in the love factor. She doesnt see you as anything less than what she most desired. Seductive beast... she is likely thinking, &quot;who cares? Fuck the consequences.&quot; she is all out wanting you. She would likely just run into the club's bathroom with you right there. ( if you did all 4 in 4 turns, then i would do much rolling after that, she is yours )<br /> <br /> Long term, I would say if you kept repeating this, those feelings would just be a natural thought, until maybe she woke up one day and realized &quot;What the hell was I doing?&quot; and runs for her life...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T07:42:14-07:00","id":935055,"title":"","content":"Yes, the interesting thing is what could happen afterwards... <br /> <br /> I mean, could the Daeva use the prefect impression during the","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T07:49:45-07:00","id":935065,"title":"","content":"Yes, the interesting thing is what could happen afterwards... <br /> <br /> I mean, could the Daeva use the prefect impression during the enchantment uses to build on afterwards thourgh 'normal' social interactions? <br /> <br /> To some degree, she would probably try to rationalize and justify her behavior towards herself afterwards ... but the strange decrease would probably feel very strange to her .... <br /> <br /> Which scenarios do you think are likely / possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T08:56:42-07:00","id":935089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935065#post935065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the interesting thing is what could happen afterwards... <br /> <br /> I mean, could the Daeva use the prefect impression during the enchantment uses to build on afterwards thourgh 'normal' social interactions? <br /> <br /> To some degree, she would probably try to rationalize and justify her behavior towards herself afterwards ... but the strange decrease would probably feel very strange to her .... <br /> <br /> Which scenarios do you think are likely / possible?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is the thing about majesty, you don't feel it before and you don't feel it after. You do rationalize it and justify it however you need to. That's what makes Majesty so powerful is that you don't know it's happening. It's too subtle. <br /> <br /> I think in another thread rose explained it something like: Sometimes we have that friend who always talks us into stupid stuff. We have a great time with them, think it's awesome, then when it wears off we think. &quot;What was I thinking.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> The high of the moment or something, you either love it or you don't. Maybe you remember that great night and keep wanting it. Each person will react differently to the aftermath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T09:54:08-07:00","id":935105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=934943#post934943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Pick up routine of a Daeva with presence 4, striking looks (+2) and majesty 3, who is looking for a new girlfriend:<br /> <br /> Let\u00b4s assume he would approach a very good looking woman he doesn\u00b4t know yet. He instantly uses &quot;Awe&quot;, &quot;Confident&quot; and &quot;The Green Eyes&quot; on her to make her feel extremely in love with him and overwhelmed by lustful sexual desire. He approaches her directly, looks deep into her eyes and unleashes his seductive beast by saying &quot;Please, excuse my intrusion, but I am overwhelmed by your beauty and I have the strong impression that we are made for each other.\u201d.<br /> Then he would make a seduction roll(e.g. presence+persuation or empathy) with an exceptional success, while continuing with the words:<br /> \u201cMy heart tells me that it is our destiny to become a loving couple with a very fulfilling sex life\u2026<br /> Your eyes show me that your heart is telling you the same. \u2026 I am going to kiss you now \u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> After kissing her for a while:<br /> \u201cLet\u00b4s speed this up: \u2026 I would suggest to go to a hotel room, to fuck extensively and to make plans for our future. What do you think?\u201d<br /> <br /> What do you think about this approach?<br /> How could she react?<br /> <br /> <br /> Which impression would you give him for the social interactions, when \u201cthe Green Eyes\u201d wear off and he would continue to seduce her into a longterm relationship? &quot;Excellent&quot;? &quot;Perfect&quot;?<br /> <br /> Which chances would you give him without the use of blood bonds?<br /> <br /> Share your thoughts and ideas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I play Majesty (figure I will go full-on descriptive as a fun mental exercise, give room people to disagree / agree / add)...<br /> <br /> <b>Awe:</b> the biggest boon Awe gives a person is a sense that they're almost untouchable, unapproachable. They're awesome, attention-grabbing, and can dominate a conversation without any effort - people under its sway become dumb, nodding sheep. They have trouble looking away. They're just so engrossing and attractive (perhaps not physically). Maybe it's just the way they say things and put things into perspective, y'know? It's not automatically recognisable as supernatural to anybody under its sway, either; it's like meeting a person with a bucket-load of likeability, charisma, and raw presence. If you've ever met someone and thought 'shit, that person can be whatever they want, they're so funny, cool, what-have-you, they're amazing, they can say anything and people still love them no matter what,' and you hope nothing but the best for them yourself, that's the sort of vibe Awe gives people. It leaves a major, positive impression, too - and it doesn't fuck with a person's memory. After that vamp's left, becoming a memory, people will still remember that amazing person and the incredible impression they made on them and their friends. Imagine a person that shows up and conversation centres on them. They leave. People may still talk about how amazing that person was. Imagine especially weak-willed people just staring like idiots. Imagine someone who's incredibly crude and can get away with it due to being likeable and popular. They might be shocking! But for anybody listening, it's just funny and unexpected. Wow! That guy waved a gun around! Only <i>that guy</i> could possibly get away with something so shocking! Who cares if he's poorly dressed for this function? He's so interesting! It's just a quirk and nobody minds! He can pull it off!<br /> <br /> If you use Awe alone, going up to a stranger, whispering &quot;hey, baby, mind if we go to a hotel room and fuck,&quot; instead of freaking the poor girl out as per normal (being hauled away by beefy security guards or male friends like a creepy pest), she'd probably be flabbergasted and amazed by such a daring proposition - even if it came from an ugly, creepy weirdo with Presence 1 statistically. People listening in would be slack-jawed by your brazen confidence and envious of the perfect delivery. But, importantly, it all depends on the character's personality and disposition beforehand - perhaps they're unattached, liberal about sex, not overly fussed by looks, naturally submissive, weak-willed, so they just end up nodding dumbly, and following the vampire like a silly little lamb. Maybe they're strong-willed, attached, deeply in love with that person, and deeply loyal to that person - maybe they're simply not into ugly guys - you're not going to convince that person with Awe alone, although they will excuse and forgive any trespass all too easily. (&quot;Sorry, um,&quot; she blushes, absolutely shocked by the brazen, crude offer, &quot;but I can't. Sorry. I have a boyfriend.&quot; She looks away guiltily - but only for a moment. She seems uncomfortable. Yet she's glued to the spot. -- &quot;I am flattered, but you're not my type. Sorry.&quot;) Mind, the vampire also has an advantage when it comes to persuading people with raw animal magnetism, and people are frequently talked into doing things they later regret.<br /> <br /> The important stats to consider when taking Awe into account, IMO, are the vampire's Majesty, compared to the person's Wits + Composure. Another effect Awe has is grabbing people's attention and making them the centre of any onlooker's universe. If a person wants to notice anything other than the vampire (or ghoul for that matter) using Awe, they need to succeed at a Wits + Composure roll - the vamp's Majesty dots. In the narrative, I'd play this out as those with high Wits + Composure able to act with a semblance of being normal and composed. For those with especially low Wits + Composure, however - say a vamp's Majesty dots penalty forces a person to roll a chance die if they want to notice anything else - those people would basically be staring at the vampire like an awe-struck, slack-jawed zombie; the type of people who would turn into jabbering morons if they met a celebrity or model. It doesn't usurp a character's free-will, though. They're aware of what's happening. Their memories still work. They can get flustered, embarrassed, and overwhelmed as easily as if in their right minds.<br /> <br /> <b>Confidant:</b> Confidant causes the Charmed condition. It makes the vamp very trustworthy to the &quot;victim&quot;. It's like meeting someone and clicking with them like it's refreshingly natural. They're less likely to be able to see through a vampire's trickery or deception; you're ridiculously likeable, charming, and most of all you have that person's full trust. However, it has some weaknesses: people aren't going to watch the vampire harm them or anybody they love with a dopey, stupid smile on their face. Harming them or anybody close to them automatically 'breaks the trust'. The other weakness is that the condition is not permanent; there's a risk of making the victim feel used and that their trust has been abused - which can be the case. I imagine most people have met someone who always asks 'can I borrow twenty dollars?' or something similar. I have a longtime friend who literally gave thousands of dollars to some random guy he met, considering him a good friend, only for it to dawn on him one day the dude was full of crap - and that he was spending that money on god knows what. Obviously, that person was cut out of my friend's life once realisation dawned. You can be very foolish and trusting when it comes to helping people out when you consider them a friend (just a fact of life, nothing supernatural about it); however, the penny can always drop at any moment. People re-evaluate relationships they have all the time. I personally have some girl I know who texts me from time to time like clockwork with 'hey, how are you' 'good, how are you?' 'i am good' 'what are you up to?' 'nothing much. hey i was wondering if I could borrow 20 dollars? i promise to pay you back on my next pay' 'sorry, i have to pay some bills and don't have the money' 'oh that's okay' and she proceeds to send texts to other people I know asking for money until someone does. She owes me $40.00 from a year ago. One of my other friends is owed $200.00. It's insane. But nobody's going to accuse her of being a vampire or using magic powers. We're all just gullible morons who got sucked in by someone (who is still a friend, honestly - just wouldn't lend her any more money) we trusted asking for money.<br /> <br /> ANYWAY! Importantly, for it to feel natural, I wouldn't have the NPC feel cheated right after the Charmed condition is resolved (assuming the character has any reason to feel cheated to begin with). For example, if a vamp uses Confidant to talk a person into giving them $1,000, then the next night or a week later they pay that person back, they're just as likely to think without being Charmed - 'hey, what a trustworthy friend, they paid me back'. They're only going to feel cheated if they're lending all this money to some random guy who gives them a reason to feel used and cheated (like, continuing to blow them off, always 'borrowing money', and never paying them back).<br /> <br /> In your example, the girl could feel cheated by having sex with the vampire. She could feel used. She could feel guilty. She could totally be fine with it and treat it like a one-night stand. Maybe she's disappointed in the sex. It depends on some context: is she the type to expect a relationship with someone she has sex with, is she the type who isn't interested in a relationship currently, what is the vamp telling her to get her into bed, does she have a significant other that she's cheating on... it can get very complicated very quickly. The fact the Charmed condition has resolved isn't going to dilute the memory that she felt absolutely captivated by the vamp, and she isn't going to automatically decide that feeling was false, and may very well seek the vamp out again to recapture that fun night. Maybe meeting the vamp again without any supernatural help will disappoint her and she'll be left feeling like it was a mistake and a fleeting thing. Speaking from personal experience, sometimes you meet someone and your first impression is so impressive that you think you could fall in love with that person, and then the next time you meet you just don't connect in the same way you did that first time -- so it fizzles out pretty quickly and you're sort of left scratching your head in confusion about what went wrong. Have you ever got a call from a girl who was clearly falling in love with you suddenly freaking out after one 'meh' experience together? That's how I imagine it. They might call the vampire, or want to talk (assuming they see what they assumed as a romance fizzling out) wanting some reassurances and wondering why things suddenly feel different or why the vampire is 'being distant'.<br /> <br /> A vampire isn't going to ignite these sorts of strong feelings in people without some repercussions. People's memories are intact. They will want to know where the crap they stand with the object of their affection. If they suddenly fall out of love, people don't just go 'oh, hey, i don't love that person anymore... oh well, time to continue on with life like nothing ever happened...' In fact, they'll feel hurt and confused, usually. They're going to try to recapture that old feeling, want to talk things over with the vamp, talk about their concerns (drifting apart, not connecting). They're as likely to be rational and try to 'work things out' with the vampire as they are to be irrational and blame the vampire for making them feel like crap.<br /> <br /> <b>Green Eyes:</b> The first thing to realise about Green Eyes is that it's potentially more potent than a full Blood Bond. That's how emotionally potent Green Eyes can get. If Green Eyes is used on somebody with the Charmed condition, it's not quite as strong as a full Blood Bond (they won't betray their domitor, that would be a Breaking Point, which causes the Charmed condition to resolve automatically). However, using Green Eyes on someone with the Enthralled condition (even a fully bonded ghoul) can cause that ghoul to betray their domitor with an obsessive need - because they'll do anything for the vampire with the only exception being suicide. Green Eyes is insane, obsessive, and all-encompassing. IMO, it's a noticeably unhealthy desire (Renfield style) to please the vampire, especially when it comes to the Enthralled version - potent enough to make the victim disregard their morals almost completely, turning them into something more base, making the only important things be their own life and their vampire's life. That's it. The flavour of this obsession is up to the vampire; fear, depression, happiness, anger, jealousy, love. It's also addictive in a flavour-sense (the feeling, the vampire's presence). Even when the effect resolves itself, the memory should make a lasting impression on the victim - and depending on what they did, they could feel absolutely disgusted in themselves, betrayed, or suddenly lonely, desperately wanting to reclaim that lost feeling once again.<br /> <br /> In your example, I could definitely see that girl seeking out more from that vampire - even if she's totally confused - just out of the addictive nature of Green Eyes, desiring to reach that emotional high once again - never has she felt so in love, so sexually aroused, certainly she'd want to feel that way again, and rely on the person who made her feel that way originally to make her feel that way again.<br /> <br /> I am not a huge fan of the Doors system, but I would say that it definitely affects her impression of the character in a narrative sense (having a baring on future meetings) and that should reflect via the system. Was the experience negative? Then her Impression should drop. Was the experience positive and does she want a repeat? Then her Impression should increase.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalty:</b> It gives the Enthralled condition. It makes it morally reprehensible to go against the vampire (literally, you have to spend a WP to even consider making a move against or in opposition of the vampire, then you must succeed at a single die roll or you 'chicken out'). It's more potent than a full Blood Bond IMO, and a victim is basically turned into a Renfield-type.<br /> <br /> <b>Idol:</b> I remember reading a few posts in the past about Idol being useless against Elders. Nonetheless, it's potent against crowds. Also, Ghouls, Neonates, ordinary mortals - they're almost powerless against anyone using Idol (usually being stuffed with a chance die to make any <i>one action</i> against the vampire, assuming they weren't Enthralled beforehand - otherwise they're just putty in the vampire's hands due to being unable to spend WP against the vampire now, effectively making any thoughts of betrayal an impossibility - really, if you're using it on an Elder with a high BP, your aim is to actually force them into a state of being Enthralled and then hit them with Idol, not rely on Idol's natural effect). Most importantly, however, there's a sense of self-preservation with every other power in Majesty's repertoire - except this one. Everybody has a 'damage limit' in every other Majesty power, but with Idol there is no limit - you can literally tell a person to sit there and beat them to death - and they'll do it with a smile. At least, that's my reading of Idol and narratively in my view why it's so frightening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 07-21-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:36:25-07:00","id":935126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935105#post935105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Idol:</b> I remember reading a few posts in the past about Idol being useless against Elders. Nonetheless, it's potent against crowds. Also, Ghouls, Neonates, ordinary mortals - they're almost powerless against anyone using Idol (usually being stuffed with a chance die to make any <i>one action</i> against the vampire, assuming they weren't Enthralled beforehand - otherwise they're just putty in the vampire's hands due to being unable to spend WP against the vampire now, effectively making any thoughts of betrayal an impossibility - really, if you're using it on an Elder with a high BP, your aim is to actually force them into a state of being Enthralled and then hit them with Idol, not rely on Idol's natural effect). Most importantly, however, there's a sense of self-preservation with every other power in Majesty's repertoire - except this one. Everybody has a 'damage limit' in every other Majesty power, but with Idol there is no limit - you can literally tell a person to sit there and beat them to death - and they'll do it with a smile. At least, that's my reading of Idol and narratively in my view why it's so frightening.</div> </div> </div> </div>First. Really great post about Majesty. It's pretty spot on to what I envision it and what has been stated here in other threads. I love it. Do you want to write something out for the Seductive beast/ Wanton condition? ( there is an entire thread somewhere what it's like ) since this was mentioned too and they do go well together.<br /> <br /> The only thing I would like to say is it is not &quot;useless' they get 'a reflexive roll of Resolve + Blood Potency minus the vampire\u2019s Majesty&quot; (say BP 6 resolve 2 8-5 3 dice) it's not great, but it's likely they will pass on occasion, But sometimes they will fail. Though that is mechanically... Narratively.. when you are that AMAZING why would they want to hurt you anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  typos... 07-21-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:44:23-07:00","id":935165,"title":"","content":"&quot; I personally have some girl I know who texts me from time to time like clockwork with 'hey, how are you' 'good, how are you?' 'i am good' 'what are you up to?' 'nothing much. hey i was wondering if I could borrow 20 dollars? i promise to pay you back on my next pay' 'sorry, i have to pay some bills and don't have the money' 'oh that's okay' and she proceeds to send texts to other people I know asking for money until someone does. She owes me $40.00 from a year ago. One of my other friends is owed $200.00. It's insane. But nobody's going to accuse her of being a vampire or using magic powers. We're all just gullible morons who got sucked in by someone (who is still a friend, honestly - just wouldn't lend her any more money) we trusted asking for money.&quot;<br /> <br /> LOL <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I thought about this as a great way for a vampire to make money with majesty without getting to much attention ... <br /> A vamp could say, that he\u00b4s doing a crow funding campain for a book, a film project, ... he\u00b4s working on and he \u00b4d need money for himself to make a living by focussing totally on this project ... Then he could just walk through a club or a shopping center and pitch it to people, disguised with some previous small talk, with the use of awe and confident ... <br /> Almost every one could rationalize to himself that giving 20 or 40$ for an interesting project wasn\u00b4t such a bad idea ... They probably wouldn\u00b4t feel extremly betrayed and they probably wouldn\u00b4t call the police or make a big deal out of it, even if they would regret it afterwards .... <br /> An ambitious vamp could make several thousend dollar a night this way, without ruining people\u00b4s lives or commiting a huge crime ... And maybe he\u00b4ll really write an amazing book afterwards! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But to come back to the initial scenario...<br /> <br /> It makes good sense, that the girl would probably try to meet the kindred again, even if she would feel guilty and confused about her behavior, ... just because it would feel terrible with the memory about such an incident without a plausible explaination ... If she really engaged in actively making love with him and making plans for their future, she wouldn\u00b4t be able to deny her personal responsability completly ... An explaination like &quot;He could have drugged me...&quot; Would seem ridiculous, because she engaged in it with a clear mind ... <br /> <br /> And, due to the &quot;green eyes&quot;, she would have strong memories of very positive emotions ... Therefore she would be very likely to want to see the kindred again ... At least to proof to herself that she isn\u00b4t truely in love with him and that it truely was a mistake.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then, the kindred could use again &quot;Awe&quot; and &quot;Confident&quot; on her and the start to seduce her again ... If she would stil resist,he could use &quot;Green Eyes&quot; again to change her mind. ...<br /> <br /> He could ask her to tell him all her secrets, her whole life story, ... all her goals and dreams and fear ... all her dark secrets and weakspots ...<br /> <br /> ... and then leave her with the memories of these wonderful feelings and the promise of a happy, shared future. <br /> <br /> <br /> What could she possibly do to resist him, even if she would have a wonderful husband and a family? ... She would probably feel very confused and guilty and start to lead a double life ...<br /> But the moment he would knock at her door and charm her again, she wouldn\u00b4t be able to resist him. <br /> <br /> Probably, her confusion would lead to tension, suspision and emotional distance in her relationship with her husband (if she has one), because she would be constantly hiding her innermost feelings from him. ... He wouldn\u00b4t understand her emotional problems and her unwillingness to talk with him about it. .... Their relationship would become worse over time ...<br /> <br /> And her memories about the time with the kindred would be full of feelings of trust (due to the charmed contition), happy romance and lust ( due to the use of &quot;Green Eyes&quot; every now and then).<br /> <br /> The only ways out would be to disappear, to kill herself or to try to eliminate him with a trap or an ambush. ... But why should she do this? - All the time she spends with him in full of positive feelings and promises of a sweet, wonderful future.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which other options would you see for her in such a situation?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:53:07-07:00","id":935172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=934943#post934943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Pick up routine of a Daeva with presence 4, striking looks (+2) and majesty 3, who is looking for a new girlfriend:<br /> <br /> Let\u00b4s assume he would approach a very good looking woman he doesn\u00b4t know yet. He instantly uses &quot;Awe&quot;, &quot;Confident&quot; and &quot;The Green Eyes&quot; on her to make her feel extremely in love with him and overwhelmed by lustful sexual desire. He approaches her directly, looks deep into her eyes and unleashes his seductive beast by saying &quot;Please, excuse my intrusion, but I am overwhelmed by your beauty and I have the strong impression that we are made for each other.\u201d.<br /> Then he would make a seduction roll(e.g. presence+persuation or empathy) with an exceptional success, while continuing with the words: <br /> \u201cMy heart tells me that it is our destiny to become a loving couple with a very fulfilling sex life\u2026 <br /> Your eyes show me that your heart is telling you the same. \u2026 I am going to kiss you now \u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> After kissing her for a while: <br /> \u201cLet\u00b4s speed this up: \u2026 I would suggest to go to a hotel room, to fuck extensively and to make plans for our future. What do you think?\u201d<br /> <br /> What do you think about this approach? <br /> How could she react? <br /> <br /> <br /> Which impression would you give him for the social interactions, when \u201cthe Green Eyes\u201d wear off and he would continue to seduce her into a longterm relationship? &quot;Excellent&quot;? &quot;Perfect&quot;?<br /> <br /> Which chances would you give him without the use of blood bonds?<br /> <br /> Share your thoughts and ideas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that is really... Umm... Specific...<br /> <br /> Alright, let's walk through this one step at a time and I'll explain how I would adjudicate it.<br /> <br /> First of all, this Daeva is walking up to a woman he's never met before. That suggests he has not put any work into cultivating a welcoming environment, so the Impression is going to start out at Neutral. With the aggressive come-on you described, I would normally rule that would drop the Impression down to Hostile. Now, if he activates Awe before approaching her, she'll see him in the best possible light, so I guess the clumsy opener will come off as enderaring instead of creepy, and I'd allow the Impression to remain Neutral.<br /> <br /> I take it the pick-up line is also his Lash Out attempt using the Seductive Beast. He's most likely to win the Contest, since he's got a decent dice pool here, so she'll probably gain the Wanton Condition, and potentially a +2 on mundane Persuasion attempts if she chooses Fight rather than Flight. And even if he loses, there's no real risk for him.<br /> <br /> Next, Confidant is going to give her the Charmed Condition (assuming he wins the Contested roll, which is a pretty reasonable assumption given his stats). That doesn't change the Impression, but it does make her trust him like a close friend, and she'll be willing to do small favors for him without him needing to use Social Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> Now, I assume based on your explanation that the seduction roll is a mundane Social action, so that is going to use the Social Maneuvering system. I also wouldn't count what he's asking as the kind of small favor Confidant would make her willing to do without a roll. I also assume he's Forcing Doors, since he's clearly looking for immediate results, which is just not gonna happen at a Neutral Impression. With 5 successes (not unreasonable given his high base stats and Awe adding his Majesty dots to mundane Presence rolls), he's probably able to open all of her Doors. So yeah, she's apparently down for some kissing. Again, I wouldn't even allow a roll here if it weren't for Awe, since the sexually aggressive approach would otherwise be too off-putting.<br /> <br /> Finally, I assume the suggestion to go to a hotel room is the one you're reinforcing with Green Eyes, so she doesn't have much choice in the matter. Unless she's had some sexual trauma in the past that would make doing so a Breaking Point, which is a very real possibility, in which case the Charmed Condition would immediately end. So, depending on whether or not this woman has been a victim of sexual violence in the past, either the Charmed Condition is going to end and he'll have to resort to other means of trying to seduce her, or she'll agree to his request.<br /> <br /> Assuming the latter, the conversation about their future is likely to be very brief, since he has done nothing that would raise the Impression above Neutral. Most likely, he'll manage to open one Door with his extremely high dice pool. Then he'll either have to wait a week before trying to open the next one (which could give him time to actually get to know her, ask her out some place nice, get her a gift, etc. to improve the Impression), or he could try Forcing Doors.<br /> <br /> If he does try Forcing Doors, she's either going to turn him down and never want to talk to him again, or (more likely, given his dice pool) she'll be intimidated into staying with him longer term. They will have an extremely unhealthy relationship, and he'll probably need to continue using Discipline powers to keep her from coming to her senses and realizing he's a sleeze bag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-21-2016, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:21:53-07:00","id":935190,"title":"","content":"&quot;Assuming the latter, the conversation about their future is likely to be very brief, since he has done nothing that would raise the Impression above Neutral. &quot;<br /> <br /> He could do many other things in the hotel room to raise his impression ... E.g. he could give her massages, he could ask her to tell him about heer life and compliment her whenever it seem resonable to him, he could tell her poems or simply try to give her intense sexual satisfaction ....<br /> <br /> By doing this, his impression should probably rise. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:35:00-07:00","id":935202,"title":"","content":"He could ask her to tell him what her innermost dreams are ... being charmed or compelled by &quot;Green Eyes&quot;, she probably would. ... Then he could promise her to realize her dreams thogether in the distant future. .... Due to her charmed condition she probably would believe that. ... This should also raise his impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:42:50-07:00","id":935209,"title":"","content":"Which options would you she for her to get out of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:06:54-07:00","id":935220,"title":"","content":"Sure. So with a little effort, he could probably improve the Impression to Good, which is usually possible without requiring a roll. An Excellent Impression normally requires work to make the environment welcoming, and a sleazy hotel does not accomplish that. If he did some prep work beforehand, decorating the hotel he planned to bring his victim to with like scented candles and rose petals or whatever, that might be achievable, but it requires planning ahead. A Perfect Impression can only be achieved with Soft Leverage, which I suppose is what you were going for with using Confidant to get her to tell him her aspirations and then promising to fulfill them.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing though, dice only come into play when the action has a reasonable chance of success, a reasonable chance of failure, and dramatic consequences. I would say that a pick up artist does not have a reasonable chance of success to convince his mark to enter a long-term relationship with him immediately after their first sexual encounter. Now, this guy's got Majesty working for him, so that's going to make things possible that wouldn't otherwise be, but they do so by bypassing the Social Maneuvering system. If he wants a sexual mind slave, it's going to cost him a lot of Vitae. If he wants a meaningful relationship with a consenting partner, it's going to take him time and effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:11:52-07:00","id":935223,"title":"","content":"&quot;If he wants a meaningful relationship with a consenting partner, it's going to take him time and effort.&quot; <br /> I totally agree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:57:58-07:00","id":935245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935220#post935220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. So with a little effort, he could probably improve the Impression to Good, which is usually possible without requiring a roll. An Excellent Impression normally requires work to make the environment welcoming, and a sleazy hotel does not accomplish that. If he did some prep work beforehand, decorating the hotel he planned to bring his victim to with like scented candles and rose petals or whatever, that might be achievable, but it requires planning ahead. A Perfect Impression can only be achieved with Soft Leverage, which I suppose is what you were going for with using Confidant to get her to tell him her aspirations and then promising to fulfill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This scenario is all kinds of hilarious.<br /> <br /> &quot;I want you to come back with me to a sleazy hotel to partake in carnal pleasures.&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay.&quot;<br /> *they arrive, entering the dingy, cheap hotel room*<br /> &quot;I know we only just met, but I thought I would make this a night to remember, hopefully improving your impression of me, by going to the trouble of preparing scented candles. I also prepared a path of rose petals to the bed.&quot;<br /> &quot;This is amazing. My impression of you has improved so much because of this thoughtful preparedness on your part! I can't believe I was so lucky to meet you only three hours ago! To think this thoughtful gesture could've been for somebody else! But you chose me!&quot;<br /> *carnal pleasures ensue*<br /> *five minutes later*<br /> &quot;That was fantastic carnal pleasure!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're welcome. Do you want a massage?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes please! Oh, you're so thoughtful!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're welcome. Now tell me your greatest hopes and dreams, my future love-muffin.&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I think if I was narrating the scene, that girl would have some major regret the next day. I can't wrap my head around a girl who would meet some random guy and go back to a hotel room with them right away. I suppose this guy has some major Presence and looks like a model (he essentially has a movie star's charm along with perfectly good looks), but it all seems too sexually aggressive to be realistic. This might be a cultural thing for me, but I can't imagine ever outright telling some random girl I just met &quot;let's fuck&quot;. Majesty is the only reason this scenario could possibly eventuate and I can still see this blowing up in the character's face. The girl would be a mess of conflicting emotions and the vampire wouldn't be equipped to deal with things (considering he's absent and unresponsive during the day).<br /> <br /> I think a slower, softer tact would be preferable.<br /> <br /> The character charms her, offers to walk her home, they kiss at her doorstep, share phone numbers, and then they part ways. That's it.<br /> <br /> Build from there. Make the seduction more stretched out. It's more realistic and builds a greater rapport with the NPC. The NPC won't be a mess of confused, WTF emotions. They'll just think they've met the most charming, fun guy -- who's insanely hot, too. Also, it makes more sense for the vampire to be more selective with who he wants to 'spend the rest of his life with'. He would probably want to get to know the woman beyond one night, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:09:13-07:00","id":935252,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1592_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1592\" data-vbnamecard=\"1592\">Jack</a>: I fully agree. The only reason any of this would be even remotely possible is because of Majesty. Which also puts it squarely in the rape category. That's why I try to emphasize that as soon as that shit wears off she's going to realize this whole thing is fucked up unless he renews the power(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:29:28-07:00","id":935265,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that probably be a good solution. <br /> It would probably work to say nothing sexual, ...just invoke sweet love and horny lust in her, engage in small talk with her and get her number. ... Maybe invite her to a board game evening with friends or an evening in a cinema. ... she will probably do the rest. ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:45:04-07:00","id":935357,"title":"","content":"I think there's a misperception here that Majesty creates sexual feelings. It doesn't, not necessarily. It does what it says on the page: makes a vampire seem like the coolest person in the room, gets someone to lend her a car, encourages him to do immensely stupid things for her. It doesn't necessarily make him feel anything sexual -- that's going to depend on the social interactions between the vampire and the victim. Most of us like and trust and use poor judgment around people we'd never sleep with, and this is just as true with Majesty as without.<br /> <br /> Similarly, while the Seductive Beast skews more easily towards sex, it's really about desire and indulgence, and that can take a lot of different forms.<br /> <br /> How this works in play depends on two things: the thoughts/feelings of the characters (whether player or ST), and the comfort zone of the group.<br /> <br /> For the characters, not everyone is open to being seduced, and not every vampire is everyone's type, no matter how awesome she seems.<br /> <br /> For comfort zones, I'll be blunt: a lot of people who are cool with a vampire charming a Storyteller character into providing a point of Vitae (with or without makeouts) are going to be skeeved by the pickup artist homewrecker vampire you describe. That's because most of us have very limited experience with blood loss,* but many have somewhat more experience with being mistreated sexually.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire</i>, and Majesty specifically, can be very evocative because of how they lend a supernatural tint to things we as real people can identify with... but for the same reason, one needs to be careful with what exactly we evoke.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* I once lost more than a pint of blood due to a medical mistake. If I felt the way I did then after a hookup, I would <i>not</i> be friending the vampire on Facebook. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:54:56-07:00","id":935362,"title":"","content":"I understand, that some groups or players wouldn\u00b4t be comfortable with such a scenario.<br /> <br /> But, assuming thatsuch scenes would be ok for the group, the rules are very clear:<br /> <br /> p.134:<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">His victim is now thoroughly obsessed with<br /> the vampire, and he can play with her feelings<br /> and desires like they were a cheap harmonica.<br /> With Green Eyes, he can shift the emotional<br /> state of anyone he\u2019s Charmed, sending them<br /> into a violent rage (or even a frenzy, in the case<br /> of some supernatural creatures) or making them<br /> so depressed that they feel hollow without him.<br /> Each shift costs him a point of Vitae, but he can<br /> instill the same emotion in any number of victims<br /> at once.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">he can play with her feelings </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">and desires like they were a cheap harmonica&quot; doesn\u00b4t exclude love, sexual desires or sexual extasy.<br /> <br /> <br /> If a certain group agrees to exclude them, because it makes players uncomfortable, that\u00b4s totally understandable.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:07:21-07:00","id":935368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935362#post935362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand, that some groups or players wouldn\u00b4t be comfortable with such a scenario.<br /> <br /> But, assuming thatsuch scenes would be ok for the group, the rules are very clear:<br /> <br /> p.134:<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">His victim is now thoroughly obsessed with<br /> the vampire, and he can play with her feelings<br /> and desires like they were a cheap harmonica.<br /> With Green Eyes, he can shift the emotional<br /> state of anyone he\u2019s Charmed, sending them<br /> into a violent rage (or even a frenzy, in the case<br /> of some supernatural creatures) or making them<br /> so depressed that they feel hollow without him.<br /> Each shift costs him a point of Vitae, but he can<br /> instill the same emotion in any number of victims<br /> at once.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;he can play with her feelings and desires like they were a cheap harmonica&quot; doesn\u00b4t exclude love, sexual desires or sexual extasy.<br /> <br /> <br /> If a certain group agrees to exclude them, because it makes players uncomfortable, that\u00b4s totally understandable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can play that harmonica all you want, but if there's extenuating circumstances, if there's conflicting emotions and experiences, it's not going to be so easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:07:37-07:00","id":935369,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if you're aware, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11546\" data-vbnamecard=\"11546\">Christoph+</a>, but Rose Bailey is the lead developer of Vampire: the Requiem. How ever you interpret the rules is up to you, but just keep in mind that her inrerpretations are the official intent.<br /> <br /> Also, I would argue that sexual desire is not an emotion. It's a drive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:21:49-07:00","id":935371,"title":"","content":"Awe makes you into Poochie.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't see a Vampire going in for a long term sexual relationship. Now a Ghoul, on the other hand...<br /> <br /> Now, the real question - is this <i>more</i> or <i>less</i> skeevy than a Werewolf's Primal Allure + Lay Low The Challenger, where they can make themselves sexually appealing by beating up your SO in front of you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:22:35-07:00","id":935372,"title":"","content":"Vampires can definitely toy with people's emotions! But the people need to have those emotions first. Majesty isn't arbitrary emotion control, in the sense that the vampire can say &quot;let anger rise within you, and let everyone within this Walmart know your wrath!&quot; if there's not a seed of anger in the first place. Instead, it's more like &quot;man, don't you hate how Sam's always letting his dog poop on our lawn? somebody should <i>do</i> something about that.&quot; And the same thing goes for sex. You might have a cheap harmonica, but you can only play the notes it's already capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:24:26-07:00","id":935374,"title":"","content":"(And by the way, vampires are creepy af and I don't endorse hardly anything that they do. However, there are limits to their powers, and, separately, limits to what players will find fun.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:25:47-07:00","id":935375,"title":"","content":"I think that the written rules are pretty clear:<br /> They explicitly state 'feelings and desires', which includes sexual desires.<br /> <br /> But if anyone of the develper team wishes to change to rule in further publications, he / she is, of course free to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:33:27-07:00","id":935379,"title":"","content":"I think you might confuse how you would personally like the players to use the rules for and what is actually written in the publication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:36:56-07:00","id":935381,"title":"","content":"By the way: the chapters of the ghouls book about their perversions they develop are far more horrifying than a vampire seducing a woman with his powers in a sexual relationship <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:04:02-07:00","id":935387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935379#post935379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might confuse how you would personally like the players to use the rules for and what is actually written in the publication.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to put words in Rose's mouth, but people are free to use the rules any way they damn well please. But if you want to know how the developer intended them to work, look no further than her posts. You don't have to agree with her or anything, just insight into the thoughts behind the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T21:33:05-07:00","id":935447,"title":"","content":"Let's see if we can clarify what you are saying (both here and in the books) with some examples, Rose.<br /> <br /> This is going to be kinda uncomfortable, folks.<br /> <br /> Let's say that the beautiful on the outside but shitty on the inside Mircalla is very good at Majesty. She spots two potential hook ups/victims: Laura and Carmen.<br /> <br /> Laura is not really thinking about getting laid tonight and has had almost zero same-sex experiences, but she is not straight, she isn't seeing anyone and idly notices that she finds Mircalla attractive when Mircalla flares up her Awe, turning heads. If Mircalla were to Charm her, chat her up and hit her with Green Eyes and a bit of reverse psychology (&quot;C'mon, you are obviously smitten by me pumpkin, let just go and we'll see what happens&quot;) Laura would be all &quot;Wow I just checked her out for like two seconds and she noticed. She noticed me! I can't believe such a wonderful, cool, liberated gal like &quot;Calla actually fancy me - oh wow how can I tell her no? I like that she likes me! I want her to like me! I'd really, really like to just let go and get crazy like she just said!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Carmen is rebounding from a break-up and would really like to find somebody to sleep with. She is very comfortable with her sexuality but pretty much 100% heterosexual, and just before Mircalla distracts her entering the room with Awe on (&quot;Looking like a Hollywood actress on the red carpet God I'd like to pull off those high heels&quot;) she's thinking about approaching a cute guy for a one night stand. If Mircalla were to Charm her, chat her up and hit her with Green Eyes, (&quot;Wow Carmen you just look so tense, don't you want to come to my room? You really need a nice, long massage. I knows exactly how to make you relax...&quot;) Carmen would feel <i>very weird</i>. On one hand she just wants some sexual release and some cuddles, maybe, and Mircalla is being a total pal offering to taking care of that with her... considerable expertise, and it's so refreshing to see somebody being open and cool about this kind of thing, really. On the other hand why couldn't she be a <i>guy</i>, damnit! She doesn't want to do that with a woman, it's a total turn-off! Nothing wrong about it but, really, not for her. But Mircalla is so awesome and so damn nice - Carmen isn't interested, but she doesn't know how to tell her no.<br /> <br /> In neither case Mircalla is making them want her more. In both cases she is making them want to do what she wants.<br /> <br /> Laura isn't looking for sex at all at first, but Mircalla is hot and (terribly literally) <i>Awe</i>somly <i>Charm</i>ing, and therefore an unexpected but appreciated surprise. 'Calla can hook her metaphorical claws on the fact that Laura is attracted by her after all. A victim of Confidant and Green Eyes <b>really wants</b> to do what the Majesty user says, and what she is proposing is agreeable for Laura, so the latter happily indulges 'Calla. Afterwards she will be probably pretty OK with what happened.<br /> <br /> Carmen's case is different. Mircalla can't make so that other girl find her sexy. She can make her feel like she really really shouldn't disappoint her, though. And make her even more hot and bothered, just not for 'Calla herself. At that point, two things can happen:<br /> <br /> a) if having sex with another girl is not a breaking point for Carmen, after all, and there is the possibility she would agree to experiment, only once and very skeptically, just to confirm she's not gay, in hypothetical and very special circumstances, she will indulge Mircalla. She will feel very dirty and kinda wrong, though. Moreso when the Charmed condition expires.<br /> <br /> b) &quot;being hetero&quot; is a big enough part of Carmen's personality that engaging in gay sex would be a breaking point for her and/or she would never normally go for it the Charmed condition fizzles out and she declines.<br /> <br /> <br /> QUESTION: what happens if Mircalla uses Loyalty and <i>then </i>Green Eyes? My interpretation of the text is that an Enthralled character subject to Green Eyes can't even try to spend Willpower and roll that die, they just do what they are told.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway in no case Carmen <i>wants to have sex</i> with Mircalla. She wants to please and indulge Mircalla, who makes her do so by having sex with her.<br /> It's a VERY IMPORTANT distinction.<br /> (aaand now i need a shower. yuck.)<br /> When Carmen stops being Charmed or Enthralled she is not going to be happy about the whole thing, especially in the second case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Disclaimer: it occurs to me now that I've written all this that some despicable people like to perpetuate stereotypes depicting LGBT people as predatory. Mircalla is not supposed to be that. She is supposed to be a fucking bloodsucker who happens to like to hide her more literal predations with sex. Also a Le Fanu reference, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","user":"Ophion","date":".  rephrasing 07-22-2016, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T00:14:51-07:00","id":935475,"title":"","content":"yes, these sound like plausible scenarios ...<br /> <br /> <br /> I don\u00b4t want to go on anyone\u00b4s nerves, but if I\u00b4d take the written rules, I could argue that she probably couldn\u00b4t make Carmen homosexual, but she could make her experience positive seexual emotions durings the sex. She would probably come to a breaking point and resist the spell. ... That\u00b4s clear. ... But if she wouldn\u00b4t , like Laura, she could find sexual pleasure during the time &quot;the green eyes&quot; would be used.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">With Green Eyes, he can shift the emotional<br /> state of anyone he\u2019s Charmed, sending them<br /> into a violent rage (or even a frenzy, in the case<br /> of some supernatural creatures) or making them<br /> so depressed that they feel hollow without him.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T04:16:37-07:00","id":935511,"title":"","content":"Personally, I always think of Majesty as the crowd-control power rather than the mess-with-single-person power. Fine control over an individual is what Dominate and blood bonds are for, imho.<br /> <br /> Though, to be perfectly honest, I think the scariest power in VtR is the Kiss of the Succubus merit. Addict everyone you sink your fangs into. And, while Majesty might not always be linked to sex, the Kiss invariably is. At least that's my impression. <br /> <br /> For Vampires, sex isn't what matters. Its the blood and the Kiss. Majesty lets you get in close enough to give the Kiss. Awe and Confidant lets you get close enough to a person so that you can go somewhere safe to bite and it would be natural, and the result of that bite is going to be the Swooning Condition. Very likely as a Persistant Condition. Swooning makes someone feel attracted to you with that butterfly-feeling in the stomache. To me, that implies a bit of lust mixed in, even if one normally wouldn't exist. I suppose one could argue that we could go with something akin to adoration and worship and excise the lust, but the description of the Kiss from an intimate physical encounter coupled along with the attraction feels like we're definitely getting a sexual component.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-22-2016, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T04:57:17-07:00","id":935524,"title":"","content":"*random thread hijack* (because i dont want to make another majestuly thread)<br /> <br /> Does Majesty's presence bonus apply to Courtoisie when substituting Presence for Strength?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T05:52:42-07:00","id":935548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935511#post935511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I always think of Majesty as the crowd-control power rather than the mess-with-single-person power. Fine control over an individual is what Dominate and blood bonds are for, imho.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for a crowd there is just the first and the fifth power. Second, third and fourth are single target and they specifically say: the target do what you ask for without a reason. <br /> I think the real difference between Dominate and Majesty is the background of the power and the fact that with majesty the orders are subject of free interpretation (a thrall could do a thing against the vampire business thinking it is the best for him), with dominate no: the mesmerized fallow the command as it is formulated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:30:42-07:00","id":935566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935548#post935548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for a crowd there is just the first and the fifth power. Second, third and fourth are single target and they specifically say: the target do what you ask for without a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, you are completely wrong about the third dot. Green Eyes specifically works on multiple people at once. You have to Charm them first, but the second dot power doesn't cost anything to use, so you're expected to be using it on as many people as possible. Walking around the room greeting people like in a party, or a performer before a crowd, or just sitting around with an intimate group of close friends. Certainly, its highly effective when used on the Carthian Movement right before a vote. And once they've been Charmed, Green Eyes affects them all with a single point of vitae.<br /> <br /> Loyalty is the only ability that's really for a single target. Everything else works on the principle of affecting multiple people with little to no cost. That's four of five abilities that are designed to affect multiple people. While everyone can play the game the way they want, so you can just use Majesty on one or two people if you want. That said, Iv'e found that Majesty as a whole is works best multiple people at once rather than focusing on a single individual like Dominate does, and is far more effective that way. If you don't want to run Majesty that way, more power to you. However, I personally think that kind of thinking is limiting and does nothing more than turn Majesty into Dominate-lite rather than fulfilling a niche of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-22-2016, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:36:10-07:00","id":935570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935548#post935548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the real difference between Dominate and Majesty is the background of the power and the fact that with majesty the orders are subject of free interpretation (a thrall could do a thing against the vampire business thinking it is the best for him), with dominate no: the mesmerized fallow the command as it is formulated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering it's actually impossible to follow a command without interpreting it (if I ordered you to akhjjklh kljkjk juhuh, you wouldn't do anything, because that string of letter contains no message you'd understand), it'd be better to say that the victim of Majesty seeks to please the vampire (which may include doing things the vamp wouldn't want done if the victim is convinced otherwise), whereas a victim of Dominate simply follows direct orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:36:17-07:00","id":935571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935524#post935524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*random thread hijack* (because i dont want to make another majestuly thread)<br /> <br /> Does Majesty's presence bonus apply to Courtoisie when substituting Presence for Strength?</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. To quote the book, &quot;As the center of attention, he adds his Majesty dots to any<br /> Presence rolls when talking to people around him. This bonus only applies when talking to people normally,&quot;<br /> <br /> Courtoisie is clearly not talking to people normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T07:45:51-07:00","id":935597,"title":"","content":"Fair. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T08:03:44-07:00","id":935603,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1866\" data-vbnamecard=\"1866\">Ophion</a> <br /> I agree that these are possible scenarios. Rose said it wasnt ALWAYS about sex, not that it CANT be about sex. Often people play on those desires and sexual desires are easier to prey upon when you are walking into a room and know nothing about the people in it. I think that's why we might default to Lust. <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> I totally agree, Kiss of the Succubus is a powerful merit. I agree that it's linked to sex as well. As it says that you dream naughty things about that vampire. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935475#post935475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes, these sound like plausible scenarios ...<br /> I don\u00b4t want to go on anyone\u00b4s nerves, but if I\u00b4d take the written rules, I could argue that she probably couldn\u00b4t make Carmen homosexual, but she could make her experience positive seexual emotions durings the sex. She would probably come to a breaking point and resist the spell. ... That\u00b4s clear. ... But if she wouldn\u00b4t , like Laura, she could find sexual pleasure during the time &quot;the green eyes&quot; would be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that you can't MAKE her homosexual, you could possibly make her heteroflexible long term with the right fostering of the relationship. Someone out there has experimented and said, well I dont like my gender, but I really like my bestfriend and its cool when we do stuff. but that's the ONLY one. <br /> <br /> I am not sure a one night stand contsitutes as a breaking point... breaking points are suppose to be meaningful. if it was your first one night stand ever and you regretted it in the morning, sure that's meaningful, but if you have done it a handful of times and keep telling yourself you should stop it, but you dont.. then I wouldnt say it's meaningful anymore. I would think the regret with one night stands happens after, not during and suddenly the spell wears off and...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T08:39:55-07:00","id":935622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935603#post935603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> I totally agree, Kiss of the Succubus is a powerful merit. I agree that it's linked to sex as well. As it says that you dream naughty things about that vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't remember the part about naughty things? The only one I know that does dreams is the Wet Dream devotion...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T09:12:59-07:00","id":935637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935603#post935603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1866\" data-vbnamecard=\"1866\">Ophion</a><br /> I agree that these are possible scenarios. Rose said it wasnt ALWAYS about sex, not that it CANT be about sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. If you go to that one Thai place that is also, unaccountably, a singles bar, you're likely to get more people thinking you're hot than at book club. And the vampire's actions have a big impact on how people respond to him. My point wasn't that Majesty is all about chaste affection, but that the effects can manifest in many different ways.<br /> <br /> (You could even have Majesty frienemies, given the right vampire and victim.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-22-2016, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:21:17-07:00","id":935667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935622#post935622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't remember the part about naughty things? The only one I know that does dreams is the Wet Dream devotion...</div> </div> </div> </div>You know you're right. In the FAQ it only says it causes you to dream of the vampire more and more frequently the longer that you go without the bite. I guess I added dreams + &quot;Lustful passionate reactions&quot; + Swooning and never questioned it when my Last story teller had my character's &quot;victims&quot; tell him about their naughty dreams. All that compiled seems very logical to have those type of dreams, but it doesnt specifically say &quot;naughty&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her craving gets stronger each night, and when she sleeps, she dreams of the vampire with increasing frequency.&quot;</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935637#post935637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, exactly. If you go to that one Thai place that is also, unaccountably, a singles bar, you're likely to get more people thinking you're hot than at book club. And the vampire's actions have a big impact on how people respond to him. My point wasn't that Majesty is all about chaste affection, but that the effects can manifest in many different ways.<br /> <br /> (You could even have Majesty frienemies, given the right vampire and victim.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been saying all along. It's a tool and it matters how you use it. ^.^ People are all very different and they are all going to react very differently with approached with certain scenarios. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> SO pretty much what you just said. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-22-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:26:56-07:00","id":935670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935447#post935447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see if we can clarify what you are saying (both here and in the books) with some examples, Rose.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: it occurs to me now that I've written all this that some despicable people like to perpetuate stereotypes depicting LGBT people as predatory. Mircalla is not supposed to be that. She is supposed to be a fucking bloodsucker who happens to like to hide her more literal predations with sex. Also a Le Fanu reference, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not like I am an ambassador for all LGBT people but I took 0 offense in your scenario. On the contrary, I think conflicting sexual orientation served as a good way to illustrate one of the issue with Majesty induced affection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935245#post935245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think if I was narrating the scene, that girl would have some major regret the next day. I can't wrap my head around a girl who would meet some random guy and go back to a hotel room with them right away. [...] This might be a cultural thing for me, but I can't imagine ever outright telling some random girl I just met &quot;let's fuck&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my humble opinion, this is absolutely happening each and every day and therefore a realistic scenario. Of course certain circumstances greatly influence the chances of success (without supernatural assistance); e.g. swinger club vs. born-again bible study.<br /> However, if you are the storyteller you are obviously at liberty to determine that a given NPC has no interest in hooking up like that. I just think that it is better not to rule this out completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:51:36-07:00","id":935682,"title":"","content":"General Question. Lets say that a Daeva Lashes Out on a Nosferatu, using Seductive Beast, and the Daeva wins. Then the Daeva continues and inflicts Charmed and Green Eyes on the Nosferatu. Then the Daeva gives to the Nosferatu his blood in order to create a blood bond. Does the Charmed Condition breaks? Is this considered a physical sacrifice capable to break the Charmed Condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:52:09-07:00","id":935683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935670#post935670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my humble opinion, this is absolutely happening each and every day and therefore a realistic scenario. Of course certain circumstances greatly influence the chances of success (without supernatural assistance); e.g. swinger club vs. born-again bible study.<br /> However, if you are the storyteller you are obviously at liberty to determine that a given NPC has no interest in hooking up like that. I just think that it is better not to rule this out completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly and I totally know girls who have hooked up with guys after meeting them that night in a bar or wherever. Mostly Animecons... &quot;hey you're cute.. wanna?&quot; &quot;Oh yeah sure&quot; .. and they run off together.. Some care the next day, some dont. ( totally saw a couple doing it on the dance floor at an Anime con.... ) I dont know if they knew each other, or just met. But strange shit happens...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Montgomery Crobes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=935682#post935682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General Question. Lets say that a Daeva Lashes Out on a Nosferatu, using Seductive Beast, and the Daeva wins. Then the Daeva continues and inflicts Charmed and Green Eyes on the Nosferatu. Then the Daeva gives to the Nosferatu his blood in order to create a blood bond. Does the Charmed Condition breaks? Is this considered a physical sacrifice capable to break the Charmed Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think being blood bonded is a &quot;physical&quot; sacrifice. I think burning down your house, giving him your car, wiping out your favorite collection of action figures is. Vampires know strange things happen when you drink vampire blood, but they dont know &quot;I have been blood bonded so my feelings arent real&quot; so I dont think that they are &quot;sacrificing&quot; anything for you by doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-22-2016, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T05:07:35-07:00","id":936029,"title":"","content":"When I read about making a sacrifice to break the Charm effect, I think of it as something akin to pushing the boundries of friendship. Asking for a lot of money can strain the closest of friendships. Urging someone to give up something important to them. Things like that. <br /> <br /> The Vinculum actually pushes people closer together, at least one sidedly, so I can't see having a bond count as a sacrifice in this case. Seems to go against the theme of the power. That said, I can see someone trying to use Charmed to get someone to drink would count as an attempt to harm if done poorly. Its no secret that the blood bond is dangerous. Engaging in perversion in the heat of the moment is one thing, but a bad and obvious attempt to control someone else is different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T07:56:56-07:00","id":936086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=936029#post936029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vinculum actually pushes people closer together, at least one sidedly, so I can't see having a bond count as a sacrifice in this case. Seems to go against the theme of the power. That said, I can see someone trying to use Charmed to get someone to drink would count as an attempt to harm if done poorly. Its no secret that the blood bond is dangerous. Engaging in perversion in the heat of the moment is one thing, but a bad and obvious attempt to control someone else is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may well apply to ignorant mortals, but if tried with vampires that know what such effect would have, despite the fake friendship? It'd lift an eyebrow, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T08:45:56-07:00","id":936100,"title":"","content":"Being asked to knowingly surrender or discard your sapience to someone else's control absolutely constitutes a sacrifice. Likewise realizing you were swindled into doing it by someone feigning interest in you would constitute a breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T08:55:46-07:00","id":936102,"title":"","content":"This is a fine line in my opinion... <br /> I dont think that vampires know the moment they have been bonded. I dont think it's like getting cut, You feel it, you know it happened, even if you cant see it. These feelings, even the first stage are like a crush, butterflies. SUBTLE. People and vampires have fluid ever changing feelings. You charm someone, put some vitae in a drink and you guys have a great fucking night. ( Considering vampires can resist the Blood bond ) you wouldnt ever know that even happened to you. maybe the night of amazing charmed friendship and doing crazy shit brought you together. Maybe it didnt. I really dont think vampires or humans would know. That being said. studying and reflecting and a vampire with occult or something might get a roll to figure it out, but at that point. Why would they care? They are in love with this person. You would justify what was done because now you love them. <br /> <br /> <br /> First stage blood bond does not make you into a slave. Ever had a crush? Do you think that is a breaking point? Ever fall in love? is that another? Perhaps for the vampire enslaving someone over 3 days to do the full blood bond, it might be a humanity check, but I dont think falling in love with someone is a breaking point. <br /> <br /> Charmed, unless you resolve it, if it wears off normally you do not feel tricked. You dont feel scammed or ripped off. You just feel like YOU made some bad choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:18:07-07:00","id":936110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=936100#post936100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being asked to knowingly surrender or discard your sapience to someone else's control absolutely constitutes a sacrifice. Likewise realizing you were swindled into doing it by someone feigning interest in you would constitute a breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodbonds isn't the same as dominate, tho. A third stage bond means the regnant has a pretty easy time social maneuvering you, but you do not lose your sapience as you put it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 07-23-2016, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T16:07:25-07:00","id":936288,"title":"","content":"Sapience is the ability to make decisions AND act based on common sense with a full understanding to where one will not act or behave in a manner the individual deems as wrong or harmful. It is not an 'either you have it or you don't' trait. And no vinculums and Dominate aren't the same but they still strip away one's sapience. Vinculums incrementally erode an individual's sapience to the the point of where your regnant can talk you into doing nearly anything in seconds. Dominate outright eliminates sapience by taking away any opportunity to make decisions and compels you to act as directed, but experiencing direct physical harm while carrying out the activity ends control immediately and self-destructive actions are not possible until the pinnacle level. And you don't remember doing whatever it was you were made to do. Majesty immediately strips away one's sapience by compelling certain behaviors even when they go against one's better judgement, are morally repulsive, or are harmful. You don't get to refuse, you just get to feel like the popular kid likes you for doing it. (The reality is they wouldn't give a warm bucket of spit for you.) It quickly erodes one's sapience to the point to where ordering self-destruction is possible. This entire thread is nothing but a confirmation of how much one can get away with forcing someone to do at a given level of Majesty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:00:33-07:00","id":936324,"title":"","content":"That's all based on the assumption that the victim in question is working with objective knowledge of how the metaphysics of the Curse works (extremely doubtful), and that the person in question is taking all the warnings seriously, and isn't an addict already, isn't talked into it through Social Maneuvering, doesn't want the blood anyways because of access to a Signature Discipline, and more. There's a lot of assumptions thrown into these conclusions that makes them rather doubtful.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the situation could go in any number of directions, depending on any number of significant factors only found in play. This is basically a white-room situation (they're not just for combat), and we all know how realistic white rooms are. Rather than trying to draw a hard line, isn't it best to make the call during play and based on the individual circumstances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T19:38:58-07:00","id":936370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty?p=936288#post936288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sapience is the ability to make decisions AND act based on common sense with a full understanding to where one will not act or behave in a manner the individual deems as wrong or harmful. It is not an 'either you have it or you don't' trait. And no vinculums and Dominate aren't the same but they still strip away one's sapience. Vinculums incrementally erode an individual's sapience to the the point of where your regnant can talk you into doing nearly anything in seconds. Dominate outright eliminates sapience by taking away any opportunity to make decisions and compels you to act as directed, but experiencing direct physical harm while carrying out the activity ends control immediately and self-destructive actions are not possible until the pinnacle level. And you don't remember doing whatever it was you were made to do. Majesty immediately strips away one's sapience by compelling certain behaviors even when they go against one's better judgement, are morally repulsive, or are harmful. You don't get to refuse, you just get to feel like the popular kid likes you for doing it. (The reality is they wouldn't give a warm bucket of spit for you.) It quickly erodes one's sapience to the point to where ordering self-destruction is possible. This entire thread is nothing but a confirmation of how much one can get away with forcing someone to do at a given level of Majesty.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2y8Sx4B2Sk\" data-code=\"G2y8Sx4B2Sk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/G2y8Sx4B2Sk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T14:42:34-07:00","id":936727,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">\u200bSorry Ephsy, but you've been warned repeatedly not to make posts like this, this is threadcrapping. 1 week suspension issued, if there's a next time it will be for at least a month. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><